# Rust build outputs
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, deliberately (WI-39462). `src-tauri/target/` matches a
# DIRECTORY only — it does NOT match a SYMLINK standing in for that directory,
# which is how this box relocates the 193GB cargo target dir onto /mnt/data. So
# the link itself was never ignored, and git-sync swept it into the index on
# 2026-07-08 (5fd810f8). A symlink's git blob IS its target string, so that
# committed an absolute build-machine path — the same leak class as the two
# docs-viewer project links. Dropping the slash covers both shapes.
src-tauri/target

# Coverage reports — `cargo llvm-cov` (P-010) and any Vitest --coverage run.
#
# The SUPERPROJECT .gitignore already carries this exact rule set, but a
# superproject ignore does NOT govern inside a submodule: `git check-ignore`
# run from the repo root answers "is in submodule <p>" and declines, so the
# rule silently stops at this boundary. Without a copy HERE, git-sync (which
# commits the superproject AND every submodule) sweeps the generated report
# into this repo. Same class as EI-22195215129102176, where a non-ignored
# coverage dir swept 74 files / +54,104 lines into the tree during P-012.
coverage/
coverage-*/
**/coverage/
**/coverage-*/

# Seed corestore reuse caches (PAPERCUSP_SEED_REUSE_CORESTORE=1 build workaround
# writes ~100MB+ blobs that git-sync must never sweep — >100MB rejects the push)
src-tauri/.seed-corestore-reuse-*/
**/.seed-corestore-reuse-*/

# Tauri-generated schema/permissions (regenerated on build)
src-tauri/gen/

# Bundled sidecar (produced by bin/build-desktop-sidecar.sh on every build)
# — including the EI-160 atomic-publish temp trees + lock artifacts a live
# or interrupted build leaves next to it (117MB node binaries; git-sync
# must never sweep them). The atomic swap renames the current tree aside to
# sidecar.old.<pid>/ before moving the new one in — those backups are the
# same >100MB class as the .tmp trees and must be ignored too (git-sync hit
# the GitHub 100MB cap excluding sidecar.old.55111/bin/node, 2026-07-10).
src-tauri/sidecar/
src-tauri/sidecar.tmp.*/
src-tauri/sidecar.old.*/
src-tauri/sidecar.lock
src-tauri/sidecar.lockdir/

# macOS term shim build output (SwiftPM; rebuilt per build)
src-tauri/macos-term-shim/.build/
src-tauri/resources/libPapercuspTermShim.dylib

# WSL rootfs tarball (~250-400 MB, produced by scripts/build-rootfs.sh per
# release; bundled as a Tauri resource — never committed)
src-tauri/resources/papercup-runtime.tar.gz
src-tauri/resources/papercup-runtime.tar.gz.tmp.*

# Seed corestore (~1.9GB of machine-generated corestore DB blobs, 50–195MB
# each; bundled into the .deb at build time from disk — NEVER committed.
# 77 of these were accidentally tracked until 2026-07-05 (WI-3065): the
# >100MB ones can't push (GitHub hard cap) and the 50–99MB ones bloat every
# clone forever. Provision the seed out-of-band; git must not carry it.)
src-tauri/seed/
# Precomputed doc_sections vectors (ship-precomputed-doc-vectors-2026-10-01) —
# written by the release cut, never committed; build.rs leaves a placeholder.
src-tauri/doc-vector-seed/

# Node
node_modules/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Sidecar-extraction temp dirs (per-pid, created at app launch; >100MB —
# git-sync must never sweep them)
src-tauri/sidecar.tmp.*/

# WI-4419 (2026-07-12): agent state dirs (.papercusp/) appear inside submodules too,
# and git-sync auto-commits the superproject AND every submodule — so any scratch a
# gitignore does not cover is committed automatically and then swept into every
# release bundle by the sidecar source-tar glob. The superproject .gitignore does NOT
# reach inside a submodule, so the guard must be repeated here. Depth-matching (**/)
# on purpose: a slash-bearing pattern is anchored to THIS file's directory.
.papercusp/scratch/
.papercusp/vitest-tmp/
.papercusp/tmp/
.papercusp/tmp-*/
.papercusp/logs/
.papercusp/bench-reports/
.papercusp/pi-sessions/
**/.papercusp/scratch/
**/.papercusp/vitest-tmp/
**/.papercusp/tmp/
**/.papercusp/tmp-*/
**/.papercusp/logs/
**/.papercusp/bench-reports/
**/.papercusp/pi-sessions/

# AppImage extraction/verification scratch — an ARRIVES sidecar-boot check (or a
# manual `<app>.AppImage --appimage-extract`) unpacks the whole AppDir into a
# `squashfs-root/` (3.6GB incl. a >100MB binary). On 2026-07-14 a verify script's
# scratch-dir mktemp failed (perm-denied) and it extracted into THIS tree; git-sync
# committed 8352 small files and hit the 100MB cap on the big ones. Never track it.
# (Verify scripts must also target an out-of-tree scratch dir and hard-fail if it is
# not writable, never fall through to cwd — see WI-4736 / the filed bug.)
squashfs-root/
**/squashfs-root/
appimg-arrives*/
**/appimg-arrives*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Vitest scratch TMPDIR / node-compile-cache. Agents + green-checkpoint run vitest
# with TMPDIR=$PWD/.vitest-tmp, so results.json + the V8 compile cache are rewritten
# on EVERY test run. git-sync auto-commits every submodule, so an untracked-but-not-
# ignored cache is committed each tick and add/add-conflicts against origin — the
# superproject .gitignore does NOT reach inside a submodule, so the guard is repeated
# here (same reasoning as the .papercusp/ block, WI-4419).
.vitest-tmp/
**/.vitest-tmp/

# EI-21266614790118256: defense-in-depth only — live-federation-gate.sh's
# gate_selftest() no longer creates this dotfile inside bin/lib/ at all (it
# snapshots into its own untracked $WORK scratch dir instead, injecting
# GATE_SELFTEST_LIB_DIR so the selftest still resolves its bin/lib siblings).
# 13 stale copies from earlier runs were found already COMMITTED here (a git-sync
# sweep landing in the file's brief create→exec→rm window can catch it) and were
# removed in the same change. Keep this pattern ignored so any future regression
# to an in-place bin/lib snapshot can never be silently re-committed.
bin/lib/.gate-selftest-snapshot-*
